{"code":"19-3039.03","title":"Clinical Neuropsychologists","description":"Assess and diagnose patients with neurobehavioral problems related to acquired or developmental disorders of the nervous system, such as neurodegenerative disorders, traumatic brain injury, seizure disorders, and learning disabilities. Recommend treatment after diagnosis, such as therapy, medication, or surgery. Assist with evaluation before and after neurosurgical procedures, such as deep brain stimulation.","jobZone":5,"kinds":{"R":{"score":2.82,"share":0.1042},"I":{"score":7,"share":0.3434},"A":{"score":2.4,"share":0.0801},"S":{"score":5.69,"share":0.2685},"E":{"score":2.07,"share":0.0612},"C":{"score":3.49,"share":0.1425}},"highPoints":["I","S"],"tasks":[{"id":22208,"text":"Conduct neuropsychological evaluations such as assessments of intelligence, academic ability, attention, concentration, sensorimotor function, language, learning, and memory.","core":true,"importance":5,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.08},{"id":22219,"text":"Interview patients to obtain comprehensive medical histories.","core":true,"importance":5,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.25},{"id":22224,"text":"Write or prepare detailed clinical neuropsychological reports, using data from psychological or neuropsychological tests, self-report measures, rating scales, direct observations, or interviews.","core":true,"importance":5,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.33},{"id":22211,"text":"Diagnose and treat conditions involving injury to the central nervous system, such as cerebrovascular accidents, neoplasms, infectious or inflammatory diseases, degenerative diseases, head traumas, demyelinating diseases, and various forms of dementing illnesses.","core":true,"importance":4.96,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.21},{"id":22213,"text":"Diagnose and treat pediatric populations for conditions such as learning disabilities with developmental or organic bases.","core":true,"importance":4.68,"relevance":79.17,"frequency":4.61},{"id":22215,"text":"Distinguish between psychogenic and neurogenic syndromes, two or more suspected etiologies of cerebral dysfunction, or between disorders involving complex seizures.","core":true,"importance":4.67,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.42},{"id":22221,"text":"Provide education or counseling to individuals and families.","core":true,"importance":4.67,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.58},{"id":22212,"text":"Diagnose and treat neural and psychological conditions in medical and surgical populations, such as patients with early dementing illness or chronic pain with a neurological basis.","core":true,"importance":4.62,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.54},{"id":22209,"text":"Consult with other professionals about patients' neurological conditions.","core":true,"importance":4.58,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.63},{"id":22223,"text":"Read current literature, talk with colleagues, and participate in professional organizations or conferences to keep abreast of developments in neuropsychology.","core":true,"importance":4.42,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.04},{"id":22214,"text":"Diagnose and treat psychiatric populations for conditions such as somatoform disorder, dementias, and psychoses.","core":true,"importance":4.36,"relevance":91.67,"frequency":4.27},{"id":22217,"text":"Establish neurobehavioral baseline measures for monitoring progressive cerebral disease or recovery.","core":true,"importance":4.08,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.96},{"id":22207,"text":"Compare patients' progress before and after pharmacologic, surgical, or behavioral interventions.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.42},{"id":22220,"text":"Participate in educational programs, in-service training, or workshops to remain current in methods and techniques.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.63},{"id":22216,"text":"Educate and supervise practicum students, psychology interns, or hospital staff.","core":true,"importance":3.83,"relevance":100,"frequency":4},{"id":22210,"text":"Des